      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Core retains; TypeScript interprets.\n\nSource bytes, revision and project transactions, six cache handles, and request/session retention move to core. Language algorithms stay in Ty",
      "href": "#m-state",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "The CLI supplies a host module.\n\nSyntax and canonical paths belong to CLI. Daemon loads the supplied executor URL and moves ordered bytes. Renderer formats lifecycle reports; telem",
      "href": "#m-host",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Identity crosses every boundary.\n\nCommandName travels beside argv; protocol generation advances to 5. Closed failure vocabularies and ordered guards own retry meaning: authenticate",
      "href": "#m-identity",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Accepted work stays accepted.\n\nCodec, validator, socket directions, lifecycle, execution, receiver and capture split apart. FIFO accepts once. Duplicate requests attach. Fetch and ",
      "href": "#m-delivery",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Policy owns limits; sessions own lifetimes.\n\nOne daemon snapshot covers output, memory, retries, polling, diagnostics and deadlines. No user threshold knobs. Worker generations, sa",
      "href": "#m-policy",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "A staged move becomes active.\n\n#148 creates package machinery and freezes CLI copies; #149 switches the CLI and removes them. Public testing becomes read-only; compiler inventories",
      "href": "#m-cutover",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
